From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] getSupportedCipherSuites_connect expects DHE to fail
 from OpenSSL to the Harmony server

Since OpenSSL 1.0.1n (Logjam, CVE-2015-4000) the client rejects a
Diffie-Hellman group of fewer than 768 bits for a non-export DHE suite
(SSL3_CHECK_CERT_AND_ALGORITHM "dh key too small"). The Harmony JSSE
server (org.conscrypt.ServerHandshakeImpl) always uses the fixed 512-bit
prime of DHParameters, so with OpenSSL 1.0.1u an AndroidOpenSSL client
cannot connect to a HarmonyJSSE server over the 8 non-export DHE suites
(SSL_DHE_{RSA,DSS}_WITH_{DES,3DES_EDE}_CBC_SHA,
TLS_DHE_{RSA,DSS}_WITH_AES_{128,256}_CBC_SHA). Export DHE suites keep
the 512-bit export limit and still connect.

Android 5.0 removed the Harmony provider, so upstream never tests this
pair. The test now expects these handshakes to fail, the way it already
expects SHA-256 suites to fail on the RI, so it checks that the client
refuses the weak group. The other provider pairs are unchanged, and DHE
stays out of the default cipher suites.

Android 4.1 port (android-4.1.2_r2) of patch 0024 of the 4.4 series,
made from its Android 4.2 port. The same change; only line offsets
differ.
---
 .../java/libcore/javax/net/ssl/SSLSocketTest.java   | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/luni/src/test/java/libcore/javax/net/ssl/SSLSocketTest.java b/luni/src/test/java/libcore/javax/net/ssl/SSLSocketTest.java
index 8c55baf41c6..008164a327a 100644
--- a/luni/src/test/java/libcore/javax/net/ssl/SSLSocketTest.java
+++ b/luni/src/test/java/libcore/javax/net/ssl/SSLSocketTest.java
@@ -158,6 +158,19 @@ public class SSLSocketTest extends TestCase {
 
         for (String cipherSuite : cipherSuites) {
             boolean errorExpected = StandardNames.IS_RI && cipherSuite.endsWith("_SHA256");
+            /*
+             * kktls (OpenSSL 1.0.1u): since 1.0.1n (Logjam) the OpenSSL client rejects a DH group
+             * of fewer than 768 bits for a non-export DHE suite ("dh key too small"), and the
+             * Harmony JSSE server always uses a 512-bit group (DHParameters). Android 5.0
+             * removed the Harmony provider, so upstream has no such pair.
+             */
+            if (!StandardNames.IS_RI
+                    && clientProvider.equals("AndroidOpenSSL")
+                    && serverProvider.equals("HarmonyJSSE")
+                    && (cipherSuite.startsWith("SSL_DHE_") || cipherSuite.startsWith("TLS_DHE_"))
+                    && !cipherSuite.contains("_EXPORT_")) {
+                errorExpected = true;
+            }
             try {
                 /*
                  * TLS_EMPTY_RENEGOTIATION_INFO_SCSV cannot be used on
